---
title: SSR and Hydration
id: ssr
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack DB SSR transports the smallest useful snapshot for the work the server\nperformed:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Explicitly preloaded collections dehydrate as normalized collection rows."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preloaded or render-discovered live queries dehydrate as ordered query-result\nsnapshots, without serializing all of their source collections."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The browser renders either snapshot immediately, starts its normal collection\nsync and live-query pipeline, then atomically replaces a live-query snapshot\nwhen the browser result becomes authoritative."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"high-level-summary","children":[{"type":"text","value":"High-level Summary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The SSR-friendly API adds six concepts:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbClient"},{"type":"text","value":" owns materialized collection instances for one request, browser app,\ntest, or script."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collectionOptions(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" creates a stable collection descriptor. Reusable\ndescriptors create fresh adapter config for each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbClient"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dbClient.dehydrate()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dbClient.hydrate(state)"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dbClient.applyCollectionChunk(chunk)"},{"type":"text","value":" move explicit collection state across\nthe server/client boundary."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dbClient.preloadLiveQuery(options)"},{"type":"text","value":" captures only the ordered result of a\nlive query for hydration or streaming."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React and Svelte apps use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbProvider"},{"type":"text","value":" so hooks can resolve collection\ndescriptors against the current client."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-router-with-db"},{"type":"text","value":" streams live queries discovered by Suspense\nduring a TanStack Start server render."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Existing apps continue to work. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCollection(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" and direct collection\ninstances still exist. The migration is required when you want SSR-safe request\nisolation, hydration, incremental chunks, Suspense streaming, or the 1.0-ready\nReact hook shape."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The old dependency-array form now warns:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"useLiveQuery((q) => q.from({ todos }).where(...), [status])","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It still works, but warns in development and will be removed in 1.0. Prefer:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"useLiveQuery({\n  query: (q) => q.from({ todos: todoCollection }).where(...),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React derives live query identity from structured query IR by default. Add\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" only for opaque functional query logic or for a hot render path where\nyou want to skip derived identity work."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the old dependency array tracked a Collection object that you replace while\nthe hook stays mounted, give the replacement a distinct ID. A different source\nobject with the same ID now throws in the derived-identity form. To reuse the\nID, unmount the old hook, clean up its source and client scope, then mount the\nreplacement."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"cheat-sheet","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cheat Sheet"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Task"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR-friendly"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Define a collection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCollection(options)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collectionOptions(id, factory)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Materialize a collection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"module-level singleton"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dbClient.collection(todoCollection)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scope collection state"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"module lifetime"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"new DbClient()"},{"type":"text","value":" per request/browser/test"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provide React context"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<DbProvider client={dbClient}>"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query from React"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"direct collection instance"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"descriptor in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"from"},{"type":"text","value":", resolved by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbProvider"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutate from React"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"import singleton collection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useDbClient().collection(todoCollection)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server preload"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ad hoc collection preload"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection.preload()"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dbClient.preloadLiveQuery(...)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Serialize SSR state"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"const state = dbClient.dehydrate()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydrate in browser"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dbClient.hydrate(state)"},{"type":"text","value":" before hooks read it"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Apply rows incrementally"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"custom app state"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dbClient.applyCollectionChunk(chunk)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stream render-time results"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"routerWithDbClient(router, dbClient)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React query identity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"dependency array"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"derived IR, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" when needed"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"minimal-react-pattern","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Minimal React Pattern"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  DbClient,\n  DbProvider,\n  collectionOptions,\n  eq,\n  useDbClient,\n  useLiveQuery,\n} from '@tanstack/react-db'\n\nconst todoCollection = collectionOptions('todos', () => ({\n  id: 'todos',\n  getKey: (todo: Todo) => todo.id,\n  sync: {\n    sync: ({ markReady }) => {\n      markReady()\n    },\n  },\n}))\n\nfunction useTodoCollection() {\n  return useDbClient().collection(todoCollection)\n}\n\nfunction Todos({ status }: { status: string }) {\n  const todos = useTodoCollection()\n\n  const { data } = useLiveQuery({\n    query: (q) =>\n      q\n        .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n        .where(({ todo }) => eq(todo.status, status)),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <ul>\n      {data.map((todo) => (\n        <li\n          key={todo.id}\n          onClick={() => todos.update(todo.id, (draft) => {\n            draft.done = true\n          })}\n        >\n          {todo.title}\n        </li>\n      ))}\n    </ul>\n  )\n}\n\nconst dbClient = new DbClient()\n\nroot.render(\n  <DbProvider client={dbClient}>\n    <Todos status=\"open\" />\n  </DbProvider>\n)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The factory matters when config contains mutable adapter state or closures.\nEvery "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbClient"},{"type":"text","value":" gets a fresh config and collection instance. First-party\nadapter option creators already attach an equivalent factory, so this is also\nsafe:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const todoCollection = collectionOptions(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions<Todo>({\n    id: 'todos',\n    getKey: (todo) => todo.id,\n  })\n)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Within one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbClient"},{"type":"text","value":", descriptors with the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":" resolve to the same\ncollection. Only the first descriptor is materialized. Include every dynamic\nparameter that changes the collection in its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A descriptor created from an arbitrary concrete config can be materialized by\none "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbClient"},{"type":"text","value":" only. Use the explicit factory form for custom adapters and\nrequest-scoped dependencies."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"ssr-flow","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR Flow"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server and browser use the same descriptors, but different "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbClient"},{"type":"text","value":"\ninstances."}]},{"type":"code","value":"server request\n  -> new DbClient()\n  -> preload an explicit collection or live-query result\n  -> dbClient.dehydrate()\n  -> send state through framework loader\n\nbrowser\n  -> new DbClient()\n  -> dbClient.hydrate(loaderState)\n  -> <DbProvider client={dbClient}>\n  -> useLiveQuery({ query })\n  -> start source sync\n  -> atomically replace any query snapshot with the live result","lang":"txt"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"During React hydration, descriptor-backed queries read either hydrated\ncollection rows or their matching query-result snapshot for the first browser\nrender. Adapter sync and queued on-demand loads start when React commits the\nexternal-store subscription, so the initial markup still matches the server.\nThe snapshot remains visible while the source is loading. Once the browser live\nquery is ready, DB publishes one handoff from the snapshot to the live result."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create a fresh "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbClient"},{"type":"text","value":" for each request. Materialize descriptors through that\nclient, preload the data needed for the route, and dehydrate the client."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { DbClient, collectionOptions, eq } from '@tanstack/db'\n\nexport const todoCollection = collectionOptions('todos', () => ({\n  id: 'todos',\n  getKey: (todo: Todo) => todo.id,\n  syncMode: 'on-demand',\n  sync: {\n    sync: ({ markReady, begin, write, commit }) => {\n      markReady()\n\n      return {\n        loadSubset: async () => {\n          const todos = await api.todos.list()\n          begin()\n          for (const todo of todos) {\n            write({ type: 'insert', value: todo })\n          }\n          commit()\n          return true\n        },\n      }\n    },\n  },\n}))\n\nexport async function loadTodosForSsr() {\n  const dbClient = new DbClient()\n  const todos = dbClient.collection(todoCollection)\n  await todos.preload()\n\n  return dbClient.dehydrate()\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This explicit collection preload dehydrates normalized source rows. Use it when\nmultiple browser queries need the same source data."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the source is much larger than the rendered result, preload the query instead:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const dbClient = new DbClient()\n\nawait dbClient.preloadLiveQuery({\n  query: (q) =>\n    q\n      .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n      .where(({ todo }) => eq(todo.status, 'open'))\n      .select(({ todo }) => ({ id: todo.id, title: todo.title })),\n})\n\nconst state = dbClient.dehydrate()","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This payload contains the projected query result and no source collection rows\nunless that collection was also materialized explicitly."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"browser","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydrate the browser client before rendering components that read from DB."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  DbClient,\n  DbProvider,\n  HydrationBoundary,\n} from '@tanstack/react-db'\n\nfunction App({ dehydratedDbState }: { dehydratedDbState: DehydratedDbState }) {\n  const [dbClient] = React.useState(() => new DbClient())\n\n  return (\n    <DbProvider client={dbClient}>\n      <HydrationBoundary state={dehydratedDbState}>\n        <Routes />\n      </HydrationBoundary>\n    </DbProvider>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Frameworks differ in how loader data reaches the client, but the DB handoff is\nthe same: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbClient"},{"type":"text","value":" on the server, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dehydrate()"},{"type":"text","value":", then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hydrate()"},{"type":"text","value":" into the\nbrowser client."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"svelte","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte resolves descriptors from its own "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbProvider"},{"type":"text","value":" and reads hydrated query\nsnapshots synchronously during server rendering:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { DbClient, DbProvider } from '@tanstack/svelte-db'\n  import Todos from './Todos.svelte'\n\n  const client = new DbClient()\n  client.hydrate(dehydratedDbState)\n</script>\n\n<DbProvider {client}>\n  <Todos />\n</DbProvider>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Todos.svelte"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLiveQuery({ query })"},{"type":"text","value":" can use collection descriptors\ndirectly. The browser subscription starts source sync and performs the same\nsnapshot-to-live-result handoff as React."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Live demo: https://tanstack-db-ssr-demo.netlify.app/ssr-db"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"suspense-streaming-with-tanstack-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Suspense Streaming with TanStack Start"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-router-with-db"},{"type":"text","value":" follows the same integration pattern as\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-router-with-query"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { DbClient } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { routerWithDbClient } from '@tanstack/react-router-with-db'\n\nexport type RouterContext = {\n  dbClient: DbClient\n}\n\nexport function getRouter() {\n  const dbClient = new DbClient()\n  const router = createRouter({\n    routeTree,\n    context: { dbClient },\n  })\n\n  return routerWithDbClient(router, dbClient)\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter adds "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dbClient"},{"type":"text","value":" to router context, wraps the app in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbProvider"},{"type":"text","value":",\ndehydrates critical state, and opens a stream for query results discovered later\nduring rendering."}]},{"type":"code","value":"function RouteComponent() {\n  return (\n    <Suspense fallback={<p>Loading todos</p>}>\n      <TodoList />\n    </Suspense>\n  )\n}\n\nfunction TodoList() {\n  const { data } = useLiveSuspenseQuery({\n    query: (q) =>\n      q\n        .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n        .where(({ todo }) => eq(todo.status, 'open')),\n  })\n\n  return data.map((todo) => <Todo key={todo.id} todo={todo} />)\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TodoList"},{"type":"text","value":" suspends on the server, the adapter streams the pending query\npromise. That promise resolves to the ordered live-query result snapshot inside\nthe streamed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DehydratedDbState"},{"type":"text","value":". The source collections and D2 graph do not\ncross the wire. The browser shows the snapshot, starts the source collections\nand live query normally, then replaces the snapshot when the browser result is\nready."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server and browser must derive the same live-query identity. Structured\nqueries do this automatically. An opaque query must provide a serializable\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":"; render-time streaming throws if it cannot derive an identity."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"suspense-streaming-with-next-js","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Suspense Streaming with Next.js"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next.js App Router can transport the same pending query promise through React\nServer Components. Start the preload without awaiting it, dehydrate the pending\nresult, and pass that state to a client hydration boundary:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export default function Page() {\n  const dbClient = new DbClient()\n  void dbClient.preloadLiveQuery(openTodosQuery)\n\n  const state = dbClient.dehydrate({\n    shouldDehydrateCollection: () => false,\n    shouldDehydrateLiveQuery: () => true,\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <DbHydration state={state}>\n      <Suspense fallback={<p>Loading todos</p>}>\n        <TodoList />\n      </Suspense>\n    </DbHydration>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbHydration"},{"type":"text","value":" is a client component that creates one browser "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbClient"},{"type":"text","value":", wraps\nchildren in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbProvider"},{"type":"text","value":", and passes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HydrationBoundary"},{"type":"text","value":". React streams\nthe promise result into that boundary. The full working integration is in\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/react/next-ssr-e2e"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"incremental-collection-hydration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Incremental Collection Hydration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Applications can also apply collection rows received through their own stream.\nIncremental hydration uses the same collection chunk shape as holistic\ndehydration:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"dbClient.applyCollectionChunk({\n  collectionId: 'todos',\n  rows: [\n    {\n      key: 'todo-1',\n      value: {\n        id: 'todo-1',\n        title: 'Streamed row',\n        status: 'open',\n      },\n      metadata: { source: 'stream' },\n    },\n  ],\n  syncMeta: { version: 1, cursor: 'abc' },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the target collection is already materialized, the rows apply immediately and\nexisting live queries react from collection state. If the collection is not\nmaterialized yet, the chunk is stored and applied when that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collectionId"},{"type":"text","value":"\nmaterializes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-gets-serialized","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What Gets Serialized"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dbClient.dehydrate()"},{"type":"text","value":" can emit two independent snapshot types."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Serialized:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"explicit collection snapshots: collection id, synced row keys and values, row\nmetadata, and adapter sync metadata from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"exportSyncMeta"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"live-query snapshots: query hash and ordered result rows; completed explicit\npreloads are included by default, while framework integrations opt pending\npromises into streaming"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not serialized:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"mutation handlers"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"pending optimistic mutations"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"pending subscriptions"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"D2 graphs or compiled pipelines"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"transaction stacks"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"module-level runtime state"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"source collection rows for a query-result snapshot, unless that collection was\nalso explicitly materialized for dehydration"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose the payload unit according to what the browser needs. Explicit collection\npreloading preserves normalized rows for reuse across queries. Live-query\npreloading avoids shipping a 50-100x larger source when the rendered projection\nis small. Neither mode serializes executable query state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"sync-metadata","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sync Metadata"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapters can participate in resumable sync with three optional hooks:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type SyncConfig = {\n  exportSyncMeta?: () => unknown\n  importSyncMeta?: (meta: unknown) => void\n  mergeSyncMeta?: (current: unknown, incoming: unknown) => unknown\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The metadata shape is adapter-owned. Version it inside the adapter payload. If an\nadapter cannot understand incoming metadata, it should ignore it and restart\nsync from a safe point."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"During hydration, DB imports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"syncMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" into the materialized collection. If the\ncollection already has current metadata, DB calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mergeSyncMeta(current, incoming)"},{"type":"text","value":" when provided and imports the merged result."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If an adapter does not implement sync metadata hooks, row snapshots still hydrate\nand the adapter can restart sync normally."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"initial-data","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Initial Data"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialData"},{"type":"text","value":" is a startup seed, not a sync-ready signal."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before adapter sync starts, current "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbClient"},{"type":"text","value":" precedence from lowest to highest\nis:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"per-materialization "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialData"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"persisted rows"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"hydrated rows"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fresh adapter sync is authoritative over all three. Hydrated and initial rows\nare provisional base state, so the adapter's first insert for the same key is\nreconciled as an update instead of raising a duplicate-key error."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydrated rows and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialData"},{"type":"text","value":" never mark adapter sync as ready by themselves.\nThe adapter still owns readiness through its sync lifecycle."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"react-query-identity","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Query Identity"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React hooks derive live query identity from structured query IR by default:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function Todos({ status }: { status: string }) {\n  return useLiveQuery({\n    query: (q) =>\n      q\n        .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n        .where(({ todo }) => eq(todo.status, status)),\n  })\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The captured "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":" value is represented in the structured IR, so no\ndependency array or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" is required."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" when the query contains opaque runtime logic that DB cannot\nstably represent:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function SearchTodos({ search }: { search: string }) {\n  return useLiveQuery({\n    queryKey: [todoCollection.id, 'search', search],\n    query: (q) =>\n      q\n        .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n        .fn.where(({ todo }) =>\n          todo.title.toLowerCase().includes(search.toLowerCase())\n        ),\n  })\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common reasons to add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":".fn.where(...)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":".fn.select(...)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":".fn.having(...)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"function values, symbols, class instances, or circular objects captured inside\nthe structured query"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a render path where derived identity becomes measurably expensive"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before 1.0, DB warns when structured IR cannot be hashed and preserves the\nlegacy mount-stable identity. The query still works, but captured values inside\nopaque logic are not reactive unless they are represented in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":". In 1.0,\nan unhashable query without "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" will throw."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DB also warns once in development if deriving identity becomes expensive enough\nthat an explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" would be better."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dependency arrays are accepted for backwards compatibility:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"useLiveQuery((q) => q.from({ todo: todoCollection }), [status])","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"They warn in development and will be removed in 1.0. Migrate to the config\nobject form:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"useLiveQuery({\n  query: (q) => q.from({ todo: todoCollection }),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" only if the query uses opaque logic or trips the performance\nwarning."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"migration-guide","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migration Guide"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"1-create-descriptors-instead-of-ssr-singletons","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Create descriptors instead of SSR singletons"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For collections that need SSR, replace module-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCollection(...)"},{"type":"text","value":"\nwith a reusable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collectionOptions(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" descriptor."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Before\nexport const todoCollection = createCollection({\n  id: 'todos',\n  getKey: (todo) => todo.id,\n  sync: todoSync,\n})\n\n// After\nexport const todoCollection = collectionOptions('todos', () => ({\n  id: 'todos',\n  getKey: (todo: Todo) => todo.id,\n  sync: createTodoSync(),\n}))","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Put mutable state and closures inside the factory. First-party adapter option\ncreators can also be passed directly because they provide a fresh config\nfactory. Collections that never participate in SSR can keep using\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCollection"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"2-add-a-dbclient","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Add a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbClient"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a new client for every server request and a stable client for each browser\napp instance."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const dbClient = new DbClient()","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In tests, create a new client per test unless the test is explicitly covering\nshared state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"3-wrap-react-with-dbprovider","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Wrap React with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbProvider"}]},{"type":"code","value":"root.render(\n  <DbProvider client={dbClient}>\n    <App />\n  </DbProvider>\n)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hooks that resolve collection descriptors need this provider. Without it, DB\nthrows instead of falling back to hidden global state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"4-use-collection-hooks-for-imperative-operations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. Use collection hooks for imperative operations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use descriptors directly in live query sources, and materialize only when you\nneed collection methods:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function useTodoCollection() {\n  return useDbClient().collection(todoCollection)\n}\n\nfunction TodoActions({ id }: { id: string }) {\n  const todos = useTodoCollection()\n\n  return (\n    <button onClick={() => todos.delete(id)}>\n      Delete\n    </button>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This keeps request/client scoping in one place and avoids reintroducing\nmodule-level collections."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"5-replace-dependency-arrays","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5. Replace dependency arrays"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Most queries can drop the dependency array entirely:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Before\nuseLiveQuery(\n  (q) =>\n    q\n      .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n      .where(({ todo }) => eq(todo.status, status)),\n  [status],\n)\n\n// After\nuseLiveQuery({\n  query: (q) =>\n    q\n      .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n      .where(({ todo }) => eq(todo.status, status)),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the query uses opaque functional variants, add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"useLiveQuery({\n  queryKey: [todoCollection.id, 'status-fn', status],\n  query: (q) =>\n    q\n      .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n      .fn.where(({ todo }) => todo.status === status),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"6-preload-and-dehydrate-on-the-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"6. Preload and dehydrate on the server"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preload a collection when the browser should receive normalized source rows:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const dbClient = new DbClient()\nconst todos = dbClient.collection(todoCollection)\nawait todos.preload()\n\nreturn {\n  dbState: dbClient.dehydrate(),\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preload a live query when the browser only needs the rendered result:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const dbClient = new DbClient()\nawait dbClient.preloadLiveQuery(openTodosQuery)\n\nreturn {\n  dbState: dbClient.dehydrate(),\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"7-hydrate-before-client-hooks-read-db","children":[{"type":"text","value":"7. Hydrate before client hooks read DB"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<DbProvider client={client}>\n  <HydrationBoundary state={loaderData.dbState}>\n    <App />\n  </HydrationBoundary>\n</DbProvider>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Imperative integrations can call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"client.hydrate(loaderData.dbState)"},{"type":"text","value":" before\nrendering instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"compatibility","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compatibility"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No existing public API is removed by this change."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Still supported:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCollection(...)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"passing collection instances to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLiveQuery(...)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLiveQuery(queryFn, deps)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLiveSuspenseQuery(queryFn, deps)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"mutation APIs such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"insert"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"update"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delete"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":", and\noptimistic mutation helpers"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Warnings:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React dependency arrays warn in development and will be removed in 1.0."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Opaque query IR without "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" warns in development and keeps legacy\nmount-stable identity until 1.0. In 1.0 it will throw."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expensive derived identity warns in development and suggests "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required for SSR:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stable explicit collection ids"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"request-scoped server "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbClient"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"browser-scoped client "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbClient"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbProvider"},{"type":"text","value":" for descriptor resolution in React"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dehydrate()"},{"type":"text","value":" on the server and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hydrate()"},{"type":"text","value":" in the browser"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required for render-time Suspense streaming:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"routerWithDbClient(router, dbClient)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLiveSuspenseQuery(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" inside a Suspense boundary"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a stable derived query identity or explicit serializable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"detailed-changelog","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Detailed Changelog"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"added","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbClient"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collectionOptions(...)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CollectionOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" descriptor type"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CollectionMaterializeOptions"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DehydratedDbState"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DehydratedCollectionChunk"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DehydratedCollectionRow"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dbClient.collection(descriptor, options?)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dbClient.dehydrate()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dbClient.hydrate(state)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dbClient.applyCollectionChunk(chunk)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dbClient.subscribe(listener)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dbClient.createTransaction(config)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dbClient.cleanup()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbProvider"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useDbClient()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useOptionalDbClient()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HydrationBoundary"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React descriptor resolution inside live query builders"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React derived structured query identity"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" escape hatch for opaque or hot-path queries"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React per-query "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"client"},{"type":"text","value":" override"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR-capable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSyncExternalStore"},{"type":"text","value":" server snapshot support"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dbClient.preloadLiveQuery(...)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbProvider"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useDbClient()"},{"type":"text","value":", descriptor resolution, and synchronous\nserver snapshot support"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start and Next.js Playwright SSR E2E coverage"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-router-with-db"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"render-time "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLiveSuspenseQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" promise streaming"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"changed","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLiveQuery({ query })"},{"type":"text","value":" can use collection descriptors directly in\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"from"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"join"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"leftJoin"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unionAll"},{"type":"text","value":" sources when a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbProvider"},{"type":"text","value":" is\npresent."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React live query identity is derived from normalized structured IR when no\nexplicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" or legacy dependency array is supplied."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Explicit collection preloading serializes normalized collection rows."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Live-query preloading and render-time discovery serialize ordered result\nsnapshots without implicitly serializing source collections."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser observers keep the hydrated result visible while normal source sync\nstarts, then publish one authoritative handoff."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydration applies rows as committed synced state without invoking mutation\nhandlers or creating optimistic state."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydration and adapter sync begin in a deterministic order: pending rows and\nsync metadata are imported before sync starts."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbClient"},{"type":"text","value":" owns collection instances and ambient transaction scope; cleanup\nreleases both."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Incremental chunks use the same collection payload shape as full dehydration."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streamed live-query promises resolve to live-query result snapshots."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"deprecated","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deprecated"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React dependency arrays for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLiveQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" and wrappers that delegate to it.\nThey still work and warn in development. They are planned for removal in 1.0."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"not-changed","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not Changed"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCollection(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" remains available."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Direct collection runtime APIs remain available."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue, Solid, and Angular keep their existing dependency/reactivity model until\nthey get their own SSR/client-provider work. Svelte is covered by this change."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query collection "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" is still TanStack Query's cache key. It is\nseparate from React live query identity."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"validation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The SSR strategy is covered by:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"core "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbClient"},{"type":"text","value":" tests for hydration, streaming chunks, sync metadata,\ninitial data precedence, explicit ids, and no optimistic serialization"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React tests for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DbProvider"},{"type":"text","value":", descriptor resolution, derived query identity,\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":", deprecation warnings, SSR result snapshots, and atomic handoff"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte tests for provider ownership, server snapshot rendering, and browser\nhandoff"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"query adapter tests to ensure Query cache behavior still holds"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"persistence core tests to ensure persisted row behavior remains intact"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start and Next.js Playwright E2Es that verify a Suspense fallback,\nstreamed query result, omitted source-only data, clean hydration, and atomic\nreplacement by browser sync"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"high-level-summary","text":"High-level Summary","level":2},{"id":"cheat-sheet","text":"Cheat Sheet","level":2},{"id":"minimal-react-pattern","text":"Minimal React Pattern","level":3},{"id":"ssr-flow","text":"SSR Flow","level":2},{"id":"server","text":"Server","level":3},{"id":"browser","text":"Browser","level":3},{"id":"svelte","text":"Svelte","level":3},{"id":"suspense-streaming-with-tanstack-start","text":"Suspense Streaming with TanStack Start","level":2},{"id":"suspense-streaming-with-next-js","text":"Suspense Streaming with Next.js","level":2},{"id":"incremental-collection-hydration","text":"Incremental Collection Hydration","level":2},{"id":"what-gets-serialized","text":"What Gets Serialized","level":2},{"id":"sync-metadata","text":"Sync Metadata","level":2},{"id":"initial-data","text":"Initial Data","level":2},{"id":"react-query-identity","text":"React Query Identity","level":2},{"id":"migration-guide","text":"Migration Guide","level":2},{"id":"1-create-descriptors-instead-of-ssr-singletons","text":"1. Create descriptors instead of SSR singletons","level":3},{"id":"2-add-a-dbclient","text":"2. Add a DbClient","level":3},{"id":"3-wrap-react-with-dbprovider","text":"3. Wrap React with DbProvider","level":3},{"id":"4-use-collection-hooks-for-imperative-operations","text":"4. Use collection hooks for imperative operations","level":3},{"id":"5-replace-dependency-arrays","text":"5. Replace dependency arrays","level":3},{"id":"6-preload-and-dehydrate-on-the-server","text":"6. Preload and dehydrate on the server","level":3},{"id":"7-hydrate-before-client-hooks-read-db","text":"7. Hydrate before client hooks read DB","level":3},{"id":"compatibility","text":"Compatibility","level":2},{"id":"detailed-changelog","text":"Detailed Changelog","level":2},{"id":"added","text":"Added","level":3},{"id":"changed","text":"Changed","level":3},{"id":"deprecated","text":"Deprecated","level":3},{"id":"not-changed","text":"Not Changed","level":3},{"id":"validation","text":"Validation","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack DB SSR transports the smallest useful snapshot for the work the server\nperformed:\n\n- Explicitly preloaded collections dehydrate as normalized collection rows.\n- Preloaded or render-discovered live queries dehydrate as ordered query-result\n  snapshots, without serializing all of their source collections.\n\nThe browser renders either snapshot immediately, starts its normal collection\nsync and live-query pipeline, then atomically replaces a live-query snapshot\nwhen the browser result becomes authoritative.\n\n## High-level Summary\n\nThe SSR-friendly API adds six concepts:\n\n- `DbClient` owns materialized collection instances for one request, browser app,\n  test, or script.\n- `collectionOptions(...)` creates a stable collection descriptor. Reusable\n  descriptors create fresh adapter config for each `DbClient`.\n- `dbClient.dehydrate()`, `dbClient.hydrate(state)`, and\n  `dbClient.applyCollectionChunk(chunk)` move explicit collection state across\n  the server/client boundary.\n- `dbClient.preloadLiveQuery(options)` captures only the ordered result of a\n  live query for hydration or streaming.\n- React and Svelte apps use `DbProvider` so hooks can resolve collection\n  descriptors against the current client.\n- `@tanstack/react-router-with-db` streams live queries discovered by Suspense\n  during a TanStack Start server render.\n\nExisting apps continue to work. `createCollection(...)` and direct collection\ninstances still exist. The migration is required when you want SSR-safe request\nisolation, hydration, incremental chunks, Suspense streaming, or the 1.0-ready\nReact hook shape.\n\nThe old dependency-array form now warns:\n\n```tsx\nuseLiveQuery((q) => q.from({ todos }).where(...), [status])\n```\n\nIt still works, but warns in development and will be removed in 1.0. Prefer:\n\n```tsx\nuseLiveQuery({\n  query: (q) => q.from({ todos: todoCollection }).where(...),\n})\n```\n\nReact derives live query identity from structured query IR by default. Add\n`queryKey` only for opaque functional query logic or for a hot render path where\nyou want to skip derived identity work.\n\nIf the old dependency array tracked a Collection object that you replace while\nthe hook stays mounted, give the replacement a distinct ID. A different source\nobject with the same ID now throws in the derived-identity form. To reuse the\nID, unmount the old hook, clean up its source and client scope, then mount the\nreplacement.\n\n## Cheat Sheet\n\n| Task | Before | SSR-friendly |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Define a collection | `createCollection(options)` | `collectionOptions(id, factory)` |\n| Materialize a collection | module-level singleton | `dbClient.collection(todoCollection)` |\n| Scope collection state | module lifetime | `new DbClient()` per request/browser/test |\n| Provide React context | none | `<DbProvider client={dbClient}>` |\n| Query from React | direct collection instance | descriptor in `from`, resolved by `DbProvider` |\n| Mutate from React | import singleton collection | `useDbClient().collection(todoCollection)` |\n| Server preload | ad hoc collection preload | `collection.preload()` or `dbClient.preloadLiveQuery(...)` |\n| Serialize SSR state | none | `const state = dbClient.dehydrate()` |\n| Hydrate in browser | none | `dbClient.hydrate(state)` before hooks read it |\n| Apply rows incrementally | custom app state | `dbClient.applyCollectionChunk(chunk)` |\n| Stream render-time results | none | `routerWithDbClient(router, dbClient)` |\n| React query identity | dependency array | derived IR, or `queryKey` when needed |\n\n### Minimal React Pattern\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  DbClient,\n  DbProvider,\n  collectionOptions,\n  eq,\n  useDbClient,\n  useLiveQuery,\n} from '@tanstack/react-db'\n\nconst todoCollection = collectionOptions('todos', () => ({\n  id: 'todos',\n  getKey: (todo: Todo) => todo.id,\n  sync: {\n    sync: ({ markReady }) => {\n      markReady()\n    },\n  },\n}))\n\nfunction useTodoCollection() {\n  return useDbClient().collection(todoCollection)\n}\n\nfunction Todos({ status }: { status: string }) {\n  const todos = useTodoCollection()\n\n  const { data } = useLiveQuery({\n    query: (q) =>\n      q\n        .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n        .where(({ todo }) => eq(todo.status, status)),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <ul>\n      {data.map((todo) => (\n        <li\n          key={todo.id}\n          onClick={() => todos.update(todo.id, (draft) => {\n            draft.done = true\n          })}\n        >\n          {todo.title}\n        </li>\n      ))}\n    </ul>\n  )\n}\n\nconst dbClient = new DbClient()\n\nroot.render(\n  <DbProvider client={dbClient}>\n    <Todos status=\"open\" />\n  </DbProvider>\n)\n```\n\nThe factory matters when config contains mutable adapter state or closures.\nEvery `DbClient` gets a fresh config and collection instance. First-party\nadapter option creators already attach an equivalent factory, so this is also\nsafe:\n\n```tsx\nconst todoCollection = collectionOptions(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions<Todo>({\n    id: 'todos',\n    getKey: (todo) => todo.id,\n  })\n)\n```\n\nWithin one `DbClient`, descriptors with the same `id` resolve to the same\ncollection. Only the first descriptor is materialized. Include every dynamic\nparameter that changes the collection in its `id`.\n\nA descriptor created from an arbitrary concrete config can be materialized by\none `DbClient` only. Use the explicit factory form for custom adapters and\nrequest-scoped dependencies.\n\n## SSR Flow\n\nThe server and browser use the same descriptors, but different `DbClient`\ninstances.\n\n```txt\nserver request\n  -> new DbClient()\n  -> preload an explicit collection or live-query result\n  -> dbClient.dehydrate()\n  -> send state through framework loader\n\nbrowser\n  -> new DbClient()\n  -> dbClient.hydrate(loaderState)\n  -> <DbProvider client={dbClient}>\n  -> useLiveQuery({ query })\n  -> start source sync\n  -> atomically replace any query snapshot with the live result\n```\n\nDuring React hydration, descriptor-backed queries read either hydrated\ncollection rows or their matching query-result snapshot for the first browser\nrender. Adapter sync and queued on-demand loads start when React commits the\nexternal-store subscription, so the initial markup still matches the server.\nThe snapshot remains visible while the source is loading. Once the browser live\nquery is ready, DB publishes one handoff from the snapshot to the live result.\n\n### Server\n\nCreate a fresh `DbClient` for each request. Materialize descriptors through that\nclient, preload the data needed for the route, and dehydrate the client.\n\n```tsx\nimport { DbClient, collectionOptions, eq } from '@tanstack/db'\n\nexport const todoCollection = collectionOptions('todos', () => ({\n  id: 'todos',\n  getKey: (todo: Todo) => todo.id,\n  syncMode: 'on-demand',\n  sync: {\n    sync: ({ markReady, begin, write, commit }) => {\n      markReady()\n\n      return {\n        loadSubset: async () => {\n          const todos = await api.todos.list()\n          begin()\n          for (const todo of todos) {\n            write({ type: 'insert', value: todo })\n          }\n          commit()\n          return true\n        },\n      }\n    },\n  },\n}))\n\nexport async function loadTodosForSsr() {\n  const dbClient = new DbClient()\n  const todos = dbClient.collection(todoCollection)\n  await todos.preload()\n\n  return dbClient.dehydrate()\n}\n```\n\nThis explicit collection preload dehydrates normalized source rows. Use it when\nmultiple browser queries need the same source data.\n\nIf the source is much larger than the rendered result, preload the query instead:\n\n```tsx\nconst dbClient = new DbClient()\n\nawait dbClient.preloadLiveQuery({\n  query: (q) =>\n    q\n      .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n      .where(({ todo }) => eq(todo.status, 'open'))\n      .select(({ todo }) => ({ id: todo.id, title: todo.title })),\n})\n\nconst state = dbClient.dehydrate()\n```\n\nThis payload contains the projected query result and no source collection rows\nunless that collection was also materialized explicitly.\n\n### Browser\n\nHydrate the browser client before rendering components that read from DB.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  DbClient,\n  DbProvider,\n  HydrationBoundary,\n} from '@tanstack/react-db'\n\nfunction App({ dehydratedDbState }: { dehydratedDbState: DehydratedDbState }) {\n  const [dbClient] = React.useState(() => new DbClient())\n\n  return (\n    <DbProvider client={dbClient}>\n      <HydrationBoundary state={dehydratedDbState}>\n        <Routes />\n      </HydrationBoundary>\n    </DbProvider>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nFrameworks differ in how loader data reaches the client, but the DB handoff is\nthe same: `DbClient` on the server, `dehydrate()`, then `hydrate()` into the\nbrowser client.\n\n### Svelte\n\nSvelte resolves descriptors from its own `DbProvider` and reads hydrated query\nsnapshots synchronously during server rendering:\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { DbClient, DbProvider } from '@tanstack/svelte-db'\n  import Todos from './Todos.svelte'\n\n  const client = new DbClient()\n  client.hydrate(dehydratedDbState)\n</script>\n\n<DbProvider {client}>\n  <Todos />\n</DbProvider>\n```\n\nInside `Todos.svelte`, `useLiveQuery({ query })` can use collection descriptors\ndirectly. The browser subscription starts source sync and performs the same\nsnapshot-to-live-result handoff as React.\n\nLive demo: https://tanstack-db-ssr-demo.netlify.app/ssr-db\n\n## Suspense Streaming with TanStack Start\n\n`@tanstack/react-router-with-db` follows the same integration pattern as\n`@tanstack/react-router-with-query`:\n\n```tsx\nimport { DbClient } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { routerWithDbClient } from '@tanstack/react-router-with-db'\n\nexport type RouterContext = {\n  dbClient: DbClient\n}\n\nexport function getRouter() {\n  const dbClient = new DbClient()\n  const router = createRouter({\n    routeTree,\n    context: { dbClient },\n  })\n\n  return routerWithDbClient(router, dbClient)\n}\n```\n\nThe adapter adds `dbClient` to router context, wraps the app in `DbProvider`,\ndehydrates critical state, and opens a stream for query results discovered later\nduring rendering.\n\n```tsx\nfunction RouteComponent() {\n  return (\n    <Suspense fallback={<p>Loading todos</p>}>\n      <TodoList />\n    </Suspense>\n  )\n}\n\nfunction TodoList() {\n  const { data } = useLiveSuspenseQuery({\n    query: (q) =>\n      q\n        .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n        .where(({ todo }) => eq(todo.status, 'open')),\n  })\n\n  return data.map((todo) => <Todo key={todo.id} todo={todo} />)\n}\n```\n\nWhen `TodoList` suspends on the server, the adapter streams the pending query\npromise. That promise resolves to the ordered live-query result snapshot inside\nthe streamed `DehydratedDbState`. The source collections and D2 graph do not\ncross the wire. The browser shows the snapshot, starts the source collections\nand live query normally, then replaces the snapshot when the browser result is\nready.\n\nThe server and browser must derive the same live-query identity. Structured\nqueries do this automatically. An opaque query must provide a serializable\n`queryKey`; render-time streaming throws if it cannot derive an identity.\n\n## Suspense Streaming with Next.js\n\nNext.js App Router can transport the same pending query promise through React\nServer Components. Start the preload without awaiting it, dehydrate the pending\nresult, and pass that state to a client hydration boundary:\n\n```tsx\nexport default function Page() {\n  const dbClient = new DbClient()\n  void dbClient.preloadLiveQuery(openTodosQuery)\n\n  const state = dbClient.dehydrate({\n    shouldDehydrateCollection: () => false,\n    shouldDehydrateLiveQuery: () => true,\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <DbHydration state={state}>\n      <Suspense fallback={<p>Loading todos</p>}>\n        <TodoList />\n      </Suspense>\n    </DbHydration>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n`DbHydration` is a client component that creates one browser `DbClient`, wraps\nchildren in `DbProvider`, and passes `state` to `HydrationBoundary`. React streams\nthe promise result into that boundary. The full working integration is in\n`examples/react/next-ssr-e2e`.\n\n## Incremental Collection Hydration\n\nApplications can also apply collection rows received through their own stream.\nIncremental hydration uses the same collection chunk shape as holistic\ndehydration:\n\n```ts\ndbClient.applyCollectionChunk({\n  collectionId: 'todos',\n  rows: [\n    {\n      key: 'todo-1',\n      value: {\n        id: 'todo-1',\n        title: 'Streamed row',\n        status: 'open',\n      },\n      metadata: { source: 'stream' },\n    },\n  ],\n  syncMeta: { version: 1, cursor: 'abc' },\n})\n```\n\nIf the target collection is already materialized, the rows apply immediately and\nexisting live queries react from collection state. If the collection is not\nmaterialized yet, the chunk is stored and applied when that `collectionId`\nmaterializes.\n\n## What Gets Serialized\n\n`dbClient.dehydrate()` can emit two independent snapshot types.\n\nSerialized:\n\n- explicit collection snapshots: collection id, synced row keys and values, row\n  metadata, and adapter sync metadata from `exportSyncMeta`\n- live-query snapshots: query hash and ordered result rows; completed explicit\n  preloads are included by default, while framework integrations opt pending\n  promises into streaming\n\nNot serialized:\n\n- mutation handlers\n- pending optimistic mutations\n- pending subscriptions\n- D2 graphs or compiled pipelines\n- transaction stacks\n- module-level runtime state\n- source collection rows for a query-result snapshot, unless that collection was\n  also explicitly materialized for dehydration\n\nChoose the payload unit according to what the browser needs. Explicit collection\npreloading preserves normalized rows for reuse across queries. Live-query\npreloading avoids shipping a 50-100x larger source when the rendered projection\nis small. Neither mode serializes executable query state.\n\n## Sync Metadata\n\nAdapters can participate in resumable sync with three optional hooks:\n\n```ts\ntype SyncConfig = {\n  exportSyncMeta?: () => unknown\n  importSyncMeta?: (meta: unknown) => void\n  mergeSyncMeta?: (current: unknown, incoming: unknown) => unknown\n}\n```\n\nThe metadata shape is adapter-owned. Version it inside the adapter payload. If an\nadapter cannot understand incoming metadata, it should ignore it and restart\nsync from a safe point.\n\nDuring hydration, DB imports `syncMeta` into the materialized collection. If the\ncollection already has current metadata, DB calls `mergeSyncMeta(current,\nincoming)` when provided and imports the merged result.\n\nIf an adapter does not implement sync metadata hooks, row snapshots still hydrate\nand the adapter can restart sync normally.\n\n## Initial Data\n\n`initialData` is a startup seed, not a sync-ready signal.\n\nBefore adapter sync starts, current `DbClient` precedence from lowest to highest\nis:\n\n1. per-materialization `initialData`\n2. persisted rows\n3. hydrated rows\n\nFresh adapter sync is authoritative over all three. Hydrated and initial rows\nare provisional base state, so the adapter's first insert for the same key is\nreconciled as an update instead of raising a duplicate-key error.\n\nHydrated rows and `initialData` never mark adapter sync as ready by themselves.\nThe adapter still owns readiness through its sync lifecycle.\n\n## React Query Identity\n\nReact hooks derive live query identity from structured query IR by default:\n\n```tsx\nfunction Todos({ status }: { status: string }) {\n  return useLiveQuery({\n    query: (q) =>\n      q\n        .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n        .where(({ todo }) => eq(todo.status, status)),\n  })\n}\n```\n\nThe captured `status` value is represented in the structured IR, so no\ndependency array or `queryKey` is required.\n\nUse `queryKey` when the query contains opaque runtime logic that DB cannot\nstably represent:\n\n```tsx\nfunction SearchTodos({ search }: { search: string }) {\n  return useLiveQuery({\n    queryKey: [todoCollection.id, 'search', search],\n    query: (q) =>\n      q\n        .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n        .fn.where(({ todo }) =>\n          todo.title.toLowerCase().includes(search.toLowerCase())\n        ),\n  })\n}\n```\n\nCommon reasons to add `queryKey`:\n\n- `.fn.where(...)`\n- `.fn.select(...)`\n- `.fn.having(...)`\n- function values, symbols, class instances, or circular objects captured inside\n  the structured query\n- a render path where derived identity becomes measurably expensive\n\nBefore 1.0, DB warns when structured IR cannot be hashed and preserves the\nlegacy mount-stable identity. The query still works, but captured values inside\nopaque logic are not reactive unless they are represented in `queryKey`. In 1.0,\nan unhashable query without `queryKey` will throw.\n\nDB also warns once in development if deriving identity becomes expensive enough\nthat an explicit `queryKey` would be better.\n\nDependency arrays are accepted for backwards compatibility:\n\n```tsx\nuseLiveQuery((q) => q.from({ todo: todoCollection }), [status])\n```\n\nThey warn in development and will be removed in 1.0. Migrate to the config\nobject form:\n\n```tsx\nuseLiveQuery({\n  query: (q) => q.from({ todo: todoCollection }),\n})\n```\n\nAdd `queryKey` only if the query uses opaque logic or trips the performance\nwarning.\n\n## Migration Guide\n\n### 1. Create descriptors instead of SSR singletons\n\nFor collections that need SSR, replace module-level `createCollection(...)`\nwith a reusable `collectionOptions(...)` descriptor.\n\n```tsx\n// Before\nexport const todoCollection = createCollection({\n  id: 'todos',\n  getKey: (todo) => todo.id,\n  sync: todoSync,\n})\n\n// After\nexport const todoCollection = collectionOptions('todos', () => ({\n  id: 'todos',\n  getKey: (todo: Todo) => todo.id,\n  sync: createTodoSync(),\n}))\n```\n\nPut mutable state and closures inside the factory. First-party adapter option\ncreators can also be passed directly because they provide a fresh config\nfactory. Collections that never participate in SSR can keep using\n`createCollection`.\n\n### 2. Add a `DbClient`\n\nUse a new client for every server request and a stable client for each browser\napp instance.\n\n```tsx\nconst dbClient = new DbClient()\n```\n\nIn tests, create a new client per test unless the test is explicitly covering\nshared state.\n\n### 3. Wrap React with `DbProvider`\n\n```tsx\nroot.render(\n  <DbProvider client={dbClient}>\n    <App />\n  </DbProvider>\n)\n```\n\nHooks that resolve collection descriptors need this provider. Without it, DB\nthrows instead of falling back to hidden global state.\n\n### 4. Use collection hooks for imperative operations\n\nUse descriptors directly in live query sources, and materialize only when you\nneed collection methods:\n\n```tsx\nfunction useTodoCollection() {\n  return useDbClient().collection(todoCollection)\n}\n\nfunction TodoActions({ id }: { id: string }) {\n  const todos = useTodoCollection()\n\n  return (\n    <button onClick={() => todos.delete(id)}>\n      Delete\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThis keeps request/client scoping in one place and avoids reintroducing\nmodule-level collections.\n\n### 5. Replace dependency arrays\n\nMost queries can drop the dependency array entirely:\n\n```tsx\n// Before\nuseLiveQuery(\n  (q) =>\n    q\n      .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n      .where(({ todo }) => eq(todo.status, status)),\n  [status],\n)\n\n// After\nuseLiveQuery({\n  query: (q) =>\n    q\n      .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n      .where(({ todo }) => eq(todo.status, status)),\n})\n```\n\nIf the query uses opaque functional variants, add `queryKey`:\n\n```tsx\nuseLiveQuery({\n  queryKey: [todoCollection.id, 'status-fn', status],\n  query: (q) =>\n    q\n      .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n      .fn.where(({ todo }) => todo.status === status),\n})\n```\n\n### 6. Preload and dehydrate on the server\n\nPreload a collection when the browser should receive normalized source rows:\n\n```tsx\nconst dbClient = new DbClient()\nconst todos = dbClient.collection(todoCollection)\nawait todos.preload()\n\nreturn {\n  dbState: dbClient.dehydrate(),\n}\n```\n\nPreload a live query when the browser only needs the rendered result:\n\n```tsx\nconst dbClient = new DbClient()\nawait dbClient.preloadLiveQuery(openTodosQuery)\n\nreturn {\n  dbState: dbClient.dehydrate(),\n}\n```\n\n### 7. Hydrate before client hooks read DB\n\n```tsx\n<DbProvider client={client}>\n  <HydrationBoundary state={loaderData.dbState}>\n    <App />\n  </HydrationBoundary>\n</DbProvider>\n```\n\nImperative integrations can call `client.hydrate(loaderData.dbState)` before\nrendering instead.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nNo existing public API is removed by this change.\n\nStill supported:\n\n- `createCollection(...)`\n- passing collection instances to `useLiveQuery(...)`\n- `useLiveQuery(queryFn, deps)`\n- `useLiveSuspenseQuery(queryFn, deps)`\n- mutation APIs such as `insert`, `update`, `delete`, `subscribe`, and\n  optimistic mutation helpers\n\nWarnings:\n\n- React dependency arrays warn in development and will be removed in 1.0.\n- Opaque query IR without `queryKey` warns in development and keeps legacy\n  mount-stable identity until 1.0. In 1.0 it will throw.\n- Expensive derived identity warns in development and suggests `queryKey`.\n\nRequired for SSR:\n\n- stable explicit collection ids\n- request-scoped server `DbClient`\n- browser-scoped client `DbClient`\n- `DbProvider` for descriptor resolution in React\n- `dehydrate()` on the server and `hydrate()` in the browser\n\nRequired for render-time Suspense streaming:\n\n- `routerWithDbClient(router, dbClient)`\n- `useLiveSuspenseQuery(...)` inside a Suspense boundary\n- a stable derived query identity or explicit serializable `queryKey`\n\n## Detailed Changelog\n\n### Added\n\n- `DbClient`\n- `collectionOptions(...)`\n- `CollectionOptions` descriptor type\n- `CollectionMaterializeOptions`\n- `DehydratedDbState`\n- `DehydratedCollectionChunk`\n- `DehydratedCollectionRow`\n- `dbClient.collection(descriptor, options?)`\n- `dbClient.dehydrate()`\n- `dbClient.hydrate(state)`\n- `dbClient.applyCollectionChunk(chunk)`\n- `dbClient.subscribe(listener)`\n- `dbClient.createTransaction(config)`\n- `dbClient.cleanup()`\n- React `DbProvider`\n- React `useDbClient()`\n- React `useOptionalDbClient()`\n- React `HydrationBoundary`\n- React descriptor resolution inside live query builders\n- React derived structured query identity\n- React `queryKey` escape hatch for opaque or hot-path queries\n- React per-query `client` override\n- SSR-capable `useSyncExternalStore` server snapshot support\n- `dbClient.preloadLiveQuery(...)`\n- Svelte `DbProvider`, `useDbClient()`, descriptor resolution, and synchronous\n  server snapshot support\n- TanStack Start and Next.js Playwright SSR E2E coverage\n- `@tanstack/react-router-with-db`\n- render-time `useLiveSuspenseQuery` promise streaming\n\n### Changed\n\n- React `useLiveQuery({ query })` can use collection descriptors directly in\n  `from`, `join`, `leftJoin`, and `unionAll` sources when a `DbProvider` is\n  present.\n- React live query identity is derived from normalized structured IR when no\n  explicit `queryKey` or legacy dependency array is supplied.\n- Explicit collection preloading serializes normalized collection rows.\n- Live-query preloading and render-time discovery serialize ordered result\n  snapshots without implicitly serializing source collections.\n- Browser observers keep the hydrated result visible while normal source sync\n  starts, then publish one authoritative handoff.\n- Hydration applies rows as committed synced state without invoking mutation\n  handlers or creating optimistic state.\n- Hydration and adapter sync begin in a deterministic order: pending rows and\n  sync metadata are imported before sync starts.\n- `DbClient` owns collection instances and ambient transaction scope; cleanup\n  releases both.\n- Incremental chunks use the same collection payload shape as full dehydration.\n- Streamed live-query promises resolve to live-query result snapshots.\n\n### Deprecated\n\n- React dependency arrays for `useLiveQuery` and wrappers that delegate to it.\n  They still work and warn in development. They are planned for removal in 1.0.\n\n### Not Changed\n\n- `createCollection(...)` remains available.\n- Direct collection runtime APIs remain available.\n- Vue, Solid, and Angular keep their existing dependency/reactivity model until\n  they get their own SSR/client-provider work. Svelte is covered by this change.\n- Query collection `queryKey` is still TanStack Query's cache key. It is\n  separate from React live query identity.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe SSR strategy is covered by:\n\n- core `DbClient` tests for hydration, streaming chunks, sync metadata,\n  initial data precedence, explicit ids, and no optimistic serialization\n- React tests for `DbProvider`, descriptor resolution, derived query identity,\n  `queryKey`, deprecation warnings, SSR result snapshots, and atomic handoff\n- Svelte tests for provider ownership, server snapshot rendering, and browser\n  handoff\n- query adapter tests to ensure Query cache behavior still holds\n- persistence core tests to ensure persisted row behavior remains intact\n- TanStack Start and Next.js Playwright E2Es that verify a Suspense fallback,\n  streamed query result, omitted source-only data, clean hydration, and atomic\n  replacement by browser sync\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: SSR and Hydration\nid: ssr\n---\n\nTanStack DB SSR transports the smallest useful snapshot for the work the server\nperformed:\n\n- Explicitly preloaded collections dehydrate as normalized collection rows.\n- Preloaded or render-discovered live queries dehydrate as ordered query-result\n  snapshots, without serializing all of their source collections.\n\nThe browser renders either snapshot immediately, starts its normal collection\nsync and live-query pipeline, then atomically replaces a live-query snapshot\nwhen the browser result becomes authoritative.\n\n## High-level Summary\n\nThe SSR-friendly API adds six concepts:\n\n- `DbClient` owns materialized collection instances for one request, browser app,\n  test, or script.\n- `collectionOptions(...)` creates a stable collection descriptor. Reusable\n  descriptors create fresh adapter config for each `DbClient`.\n- `dbClient.dehydrate()`, `dbClient.hydrate(state)`, and\n  `dbClient.applyCollectionChunk(chunk)` move explicit collection state across\n  the server/client boundary.\n- `dbClient.preloadLiveQuery(options)` captures only the ordered result of a\n  live query for hydration or streaming.\n- React and Svelte apps use `DbProvider` so hooks can resolve collection\n  descriptors against the current client.\n- `@tanstack/react-router-with-db` streams live queries discovered by Suspense\n  during a TanStack Start server render.\n\nExisting apps continue to work. `createCollection(...)` and direct collection\ninstances still exist. The migration is required when you want SSR-safe request\nisolation, hydration, incremental chunks, Suspense streaming, or the 1.0-ready\nReact hook shape.\n\nThe old dependency-array form now warns:\n\n```tsx\nuseLiveQuery((q) => q.from({ todos }).where(...), [status])\n```\n\nIt still works, but warns in development and will be removed in 1.0. Prefer:\n\n```tsx\nuseLiveQuery({\n  query: (q) => q.from({ todos: todoCollection }).where(...),\n})\n```\n\nReact derives live query identity from structured query IR by default. Add\n`queryKey` only for opaque functional query logic or for a hot render path where\nyou want to skip derived identity work.\n\nIf the old dependency array tracked a Collection object that you replace while\nthe hook stays mounted, give the replacement a distinct ID. A different source\nobject with the same ID now throws in the derived-identity form. To reuse the\nID, unmount the old hook, clean up its source and client scope, then mount the\nreplacement.\n\n## Cheat Sheet\n\n| Task | Before | SSR-friendly |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Define a collection | `createCollection(options)` | `collectionOptions(id, factory)` |\n| Materialize a collection | module-level singleton | `dbClient.collection(todoCollection)` |\n| Scope collection state | module lifetime | `new DbClient()` per request/browser/test |\n| Provide React context | none | `<DbProvider client={dbClient}>` |\n| Query from React | direct collection instance | descriptor in `from`, resolved by `DbProvider` |\n| Mutate from React | import singleton collection | `useDbClient().collection(todoCollection)` |\n| Server preload | ad hoc collection preload | `collection.preload()` or `dbClient.preloadLiveQuery(...)` |\n| Serialize SSR state | none | `const state = dbClient.dehydrate()` |\n| Hydrate in browser | none | `dbClient.hydrate(state)` before hooks read it |\n| Apply rows incrementally | custom app state | `dbClient.applyCollectionChunk(chunk)` |\n| Stream render-time results | none | `routerWithDbClient(router, dbClient)` |\n| React query identity | dependency array | derived IR, or `queryKey` when needed |\n\n### Minimal React Pattern\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  DbClient,\n  DbProvider,\n  collectionOptions,\n  eq,\n  useDbClient,\n  useLiveQuery,\n} from '@tanstack/react-db'\n\nconst todoCollection = collectionOptions('todos', () => ({\n  id: 'todos',\n  getKey: (todo: Todo) => todo.id,\n  sync: {\n    sync: ({ markReady }) => {\n      markReady()\n    },\n  },\n}))\n\nfunction useTodoCollection() {\n  return useDbClient().collection(todoCollection)\n}\n\nfunction Todos({ status }: { status: string }) {\n  const todos = useTodoCollection()\n\n  const { data } = useLiveQuery({\n    query: (q) =>\n      q\n        .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n        .where(({ todo }) => eq(todo.status, status)),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <ul>\n      {data.map((todo) => (\n        <li\n          key={todo.id}\n          onClick={() => todos.update(todo.id, (draft) => {\n            draft.done = true\n          })}\n        >\n          {todo.title}\n        </li>\n      ))}\n    </ul>\n  )\n}\n\nconst dbClient = new DbClient()\n\nroot.render(\n  <DbProvider client={dbClient}>\n    <Todos status=\"open\" />\n  </DbProvider>\n)\n```\n\nThe factory matters when config contains mutable adapter state or closures.\nEvery `DbClient` gets a fresh config and collection instance. First-party\nadapter option creators already attach an equivalent factory, so this is also\nsafe:\n\n```tsx\nconst todoCollection = collectionOptions(\n  localOnlyCollectionOptions<Todo>({\n    id: 'todos',\n    getKey: (todo) => todo.id,\n  })\n)\n```\n\nWithin one `DbClient`, descriptors with the same `id` resolve to the same\ncollection. Only the first descriptor is materialized. Include every dynamic\nparameter that changes the collection in its `id`.\n\nA descriptor created from an arbitrary concrete config can be materialized by\none `DbClient` only. Use the explicit factory form for custom adapters and\nrequest-scoped dependencies.\n\n## SSR Flow\n\nThe server and browser use the same descriptors, but different `DbClient`\ninstances.\n\n```txt\nserver request\n  -> new DbClient()\n  -> preload an explicit collection or live-query result\n  -> dbClient.dehydrate()\n  -> send state through framework loader\n\nbrowser\n  -> new DbClient()\n  -> dbClient.hydrate(loaderState)\n  -> <DbProvider client={dbClient}>\n  -> useLiveQuery({ query })\n  -> start source sync\n  -> atomically replace any query snapshot with the live result\n```\n\nDuring React hydration, descriptor-backed queries read either hydrated\ncollection rows or their matching query-result snapshot for the first browser\nrender. Adapter sync and queued on-demand loads start when React commits the\nexternal-store subscription, so the initial markup still matches the server.\nThe snapshot remains visible while the source is loading. Once the browser live\nquery is ready, DB publishes one handoff from the snapshot to the live result.\n\n### Server\n\nCreate a fresh `DbClient` for each request. Materialize descriptors through that\nclient, preload the data needed for the route, and dehydrate the client.\n\n```tsx\nimport { DbClient, collectionOptions, eq } from '@tanstack/db'\n\nexport const todoCollection = collectionOptions('todos', () => ({\n  id: 'todos',\n  getKey: (todo: Todo) => todo.id,\n  syncMode: 'on-demand',\n  sync: {\n    sync: ({ markReady, begin, write, commit }) => {\n      markReady()\n\n      return {\n        loadSubset: async () => {\n          const todos = await api.todos.list()\n          begin()\n          for (const todo of todos) {\n            write({ type: 'insert', value: todo })\n          }\n          commit()\n          return true\n        },\n      }\n    },\n  },\n}))\n\nexport async function loadTodosForSsr() {\n  const dbClient = new DbClient()\n  const todos = dbClient.collection(todoCollection)\n  await todos.preload()\n\n  return dbClient.dehydrate()\n}\n```\n\nThis explicit collection preload dehydrates normalized source rows. Use it when\nmultiple browser queries need the same source data.\n\nIf the source is much larger than the rendered result, preload the query instead:\n\n```tsx\nconst dbClient = new DbClient()\n\nawait dbClient.preloadLiveQuery({\n  query: (q) =>\n    q\n      .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n      .where(({ todo }) => eq(todo.status, 'open'))\n      .select(({ todo }) => ({ id: todo.id, title: todo.title })),\n})\n\nconst state = dbClient.dehydrate()\n```\n\nThis payload contains the projected query result and no source collection rows\nunless that collection was also materialized explicitly.\n\n### Browser\n\nHydrate the browser client before rendering components that read from DB.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  DbClient,\n  DbProvider,\n  HydrationBoundary,\n} from '@tanstack/react-db'\n\nfunction App({ dehydratedDbState }: { dehydratedDbState: DehydratedDbState }) {\n  const [dbClient] = React.useState(() => new DbClient())\n\n  return (\n    <DbProvider client={dbClient}>\n      <HydrationBoundary state={dehydratedDbState}>\n        <Routes />\n      </HydrationBoundary>\n    </DbProvider>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nFrameworks differ in how loader data reaches the client, but the DB handoff is\nthe same: `DbClient` on the server, `dehydrate()`, then `hydrate()` into the\nbrowser client.\n\n### Svelte\n\nSvelte resolves descriptors from its own `DbProvider` and reads hydrated query\nsnapshots synchronously during server rendering:\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { DbClient, DbProvider } from '@tanstack/svelte-db'\n  import Todos from './Todos.svelte'\n\n  const client = new DbClient()\n  client.hydrate(dehydratedDbState)\n</script>\n\n<DbProvider {client}>\n  <Todos />\n</DbProvider>\n```\n\nInside `Todos.svelte`, `useLiveQuery({ query })` can use collection descriptors\ndirectly. The browser subscription starts source sync and performs the same\nsnapshot-to-live-result handoff as React.\n\nLive demo: https://tanstack-db-ssr-demo.netlify.app/ssr-db\n\n## Suspense Streaming with TanStack Start\n\n`@tanstack/react-router-with-db` follows the same integration pattern as\n`@tanstack/react-router-with-query`:\n\n```tsx\nimport { DbClient } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { routerWithDbClient } from '@tanstack/react-router-with-db'\n\nexport type RouterContext = {\n  dbClient: DbClient\n}\n\nexport function getRouter() {\n  const dbClient = new DbClient()\n  const router = createRouter({\n    routeTree,\n    context: { dbClient },\n  })\n\n  return routerWithDbClient(router, dbClient)\n}\n```\n\nThe adapter adds `dbClient` to router context, wraps the app in `DbProvider`,\ndehydrates critical state, and opens a stream for query results discovered later\nduring rendering.\n\n```tsx\nfunction RouteComponent() {\n  return (\n    <Suspense fallback={<p>Loading todos</p>}>\n      <TodoList />\n    </Suspense>\n  )\n}\n\nfunction TodoList() {\n  const { data } = useLiveSuspenseQuery({\n    query: (q) =>\n      q\n        .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n        .where(({ todo }) => eq(todo.status, 'open')),\n  })\n\n  return data.map((todo) => <Todo key={todo.id} todo={todo} />)\n}\n```\n\nWhen `TodoList` suspends on the server, the adapter streams the pending query\npromise. That promise resolves to the ordered live-query result snapshot inside\nthe streamed `DehydratedDbState`. The source collections and D2 graph do not\ncross the wire. The browser shows the snapshot, starts the source collections\nand live query normally, then replaces the snapshot when the browser result is\nready.\n\nThe server and browser must derive the same live-query identity. Structured\nqueries do this automatically. An opaque query must provide a serializable\n`queryKey`; render-time streaming throws if it cannot derive an identity.\n\n## Suspense Streaming with Next.js\n\nNext.js App Router can transport the same pending query promise through React\nServer Components. Start the preload without awaiting it, dehydrate the pending\nresult, and pass that state to a client hydration boundary:\n\n```tsx\nexport default function Page() {\n  const dbClient = new DbClient()\n  void dbClient.preloadLiveQuery(openTodosQuery)\n\n  const state = dbClient.dehydrate({\n    shouldDehydrateCollection: () => false,\n    shouldDehydrateLiveQuery: () => true,\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <DbHydration state={state}>\n      <Suspense fallback={<p>Loading todos</p>}>\n        <TodoList />\n      </Suspense>\n    </DbHydration>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n`DbHydration` is a client component that creates one browser `DbClient`, wraps\nchildren in `DbProvider`, and passes `state` to `HydrationBoundary`. React streams\nthe promise result into that boundary. The full working integration is in\n`examples/react/next-ssr-e2e`.\n\n## Incremental Collection Hydration\n\nApplications can also apply collection rows received through their own stream.\nIncremental hydration uses the same collection chunk shape as holistic\ndehydration:\n\n```ts\ndbClient.applyCollectionChunk({\n  collectionId: 'todos',\n  rows: [\n    {\n      key: 'todo-1',\n      value: {\n        id: 'todo-1',\n        title: 'Streamed row',\n        status: 'open',\n      },\n      metadata: { source: 'stream' },\n    },\n  ],\n  syncMeta: { version: 1, cursor: 'abc' },\n})\n```\n\nIf the target collection is already materialized, the rows apply immediately and\nexisting live queries react from collection state. If the collection is not\nmaterialized yet, the chunk is stored and applied when that `collectionId`\nmaterializes.\n\n## What Gets Serialized\n\n`dbClient.dehydrate()` can emit two independent snapshot types.\n\nSerialized:\n\n- explicit collection snapshots: collection id, synced row keys and values, row\n  metadata, and adapter sync metadata from `exportSyncMeta`\n- live-query snapshots: query hash and ordered result rows; completed explicit\n  preloads are included by default, while framework integrations opt pending\n  promises into streaming\n\nNot serialized:\n\n- mutation handlers\n- pending optimistic mutations\n- pending subscriptions\n- D2 graphs or compiled pipelines\n- transaction stacks\n- module-level runtime state\n- source collection rows for a query-result snapshot, unless that collection was\n  also explicitly materialized for dehydration\n\nChoose the payload unit according to what the browser needs. Explicit collection\npreloading preserves normalized rows for reuse across queries. Live-query\npreloading avoids shipping a 50-100x larger source when the rendered projection\nis small. Neither mode serializes executable query state.\n\n## Sync Metadata\n\nAdapters can participate in resumable sync with three optional hooks:\n\n```ts\ntype SyncConfig = {\n  exportSyncMeta?: () => unknown\n  importSyncMeta?: (meta: unknown) => void\n  mergeSyncMeta?: (current: unknown, incoming: unknown) => unknown\n}\n```\n\nThe metadata shape is adapter-owned. Version it inside the adapter payload. If an\nadapter cannot understand incoming metadata, it should ignore it and restart\nsync from a safe point.\n\nDuring hydration, DB imports `syncMeta` into the materialized collection. If the\ncollection already has current metadata, DB calls `mergeSyncMeta(current,\nincoming)` when provided and imports the merged result.\n\nIf an adapter does not implement sync metadata hooks, row snapshots still hydrate\nand the adapter can restart sync normally.\n\n## Initial Data\n\n`initialData` is a startup seed, not a sync-ready signal.\n\nBefore adapter sync starts, current `DbClient` precedence from lowest to highest\nis:\n\n1. per-materialization `initialData`\n2. persisted rows\n3. hydrated rows\n\nFresh adapter sync is authoritative over all three. Hydrated and initial rows\nare provisional base state, so the adapter's first insert for the same key is\nreconciled as an update instead of raising a duplicate-key error.\n\nHydrated rows and `initialData` never mark adapter sync as ready by themselves.\nThe adapter still owns readiness through its sync lifecycle.\n\n## React Query Identity\n\nReact hooks derive live query identity from structured query IR by default:\n\n```tsx\nfunction Todos({ status }: { status: string }) {\n  return useLiveQuery({\n    query: (q) =>\n      q\n        .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n        .where(({ todo }) => eq(todo.status, status)),\n  })\n}\n```\n\nThe captured `status` value is represented in the structured IR, so no\ndependency array or `queryKey` is required.\n\nUse `queryKey` when the query contains opaque runtime logic that DB cannot\nstably represent:\n\n```tsx\nfunction SearchTodos({ search }: { search: string }) {\n  return useLiveQuery({\n    queryKey: [todoCollection.id, 'search', search],\n    query: (q) =>\n      q\n        .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n        .fn.where(({ todo }) =>\n          todo.title.toLowerCase().includes(search.toLowerCase())\n        ),\n  })\n}\n```\n\nCommon reasons to add `queryKey`:\n\n- `.fn.where(...)`\n- `.fn.select(...)`\n- `.fn.having(...)`\n- function values, symbols, class instances, or circular objects captured inside\n  the structured query\n- a render path where derived identity becomes measurably expensive\n\nBefore 1.0, DB warns when structured IR cannot be hashed and preserves the\nlegacy mount-stable identity. The query still works, but captured values inside\nopaque logic are not reactive unless they are represented in `queryKey`. In 1.0,\nan unhashable query without `queryKey` will throw.\n\nDB also warns once in development if deriving identity becomes expensive enough\nthat an explicit `queryKey` would be better.\n\nDependency arrays are accepted for backwards compatibility:\n\n```tsx\nuseLiveQuery((q) => q.from({ todo: todoCollection }), [status])\n```\n\nThey warn in development and will be removed in 1.0. Migrate to the config\nobject form:\n\n```tsx\nuseLiveQuery({\n  query: (q) => q.from({ todo: todoCollection }),\n})\n```\n\nAdd `queryKey` only if the query uses opaque logic or trips the performance\nwarning.\n\n## Migration Guide\n\n### 1. Create descriptors instead of SSR singletons\n\nFor collections that need SSR, replace module-level `createCollection(...)`\nwith a reusable `collectionOptions(...)` descriptor.\n\n```tsx\n// Before\nexport const todoCollection = createCollection({\n  id: 'todos',\n  getKey: (todo) => todo.id,\n  sync: todoSync,\n})\n\n// After\nexport const todoCollection = collectionOptions('todos', () => ({\n  id: 'todos',\n  getKey: (todo: Todo) => todo.id,\n  sync: createTodoSync(),\n}))\n```\n\nPut mutable state and closures inside the factory. First-party adapter option\ncreators can also be passed directly because they provide a fresh config\nfactory. Collections that never participate in SSR can keep using\n`createCollection`.\n\n### 2. Add a `DbClient`\n\nUse a new client for every server request and a stable client for each browser\napp instance.\n\n```tsx\nconst dbClient = new DbClient()\n```\n\nIn tests, create a new client per test unless the test is explicitly covering\nshared state.\n\n### 3. Wrap React with `DbProvider`\n\n```tsx\nroot.render(\n  <DbProvider client={dbClient}>\n    <App />\n  </DbProvider>\n)\n```\n\nHooks that resolve collection descriptors need this provider. Without it, DB\nthrows instead of falling back to hidden global state.\n\n### 4. Use collection hooks for imperative operations\n\nUse descriptors directly in live query sources, and materialize only when you\nneed collection methods:\n\n```tsx\nfunction useTodoCollection() {\n  return useDbClient().collection(todoCollection)\n}\n\nfunction TodoActions({ id }: { id: string }) {\n  const todos = useTodoCollection()\n\n  return (\n    <button onClick={() => todos.delete(id)}>\n      Delete\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThis keeps request/client scoping in one place and avoids reintroducing\nmodule-level collections.\n\n### 5. Replace dependency arrays\n\nMost queries can drop the dependency array entirely:\n\n```tsx\n// Before\nuseLiveQuery(\n  (q) =>\n    q\n      .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n      .where(({ todo }) => eq(todo.status, status)),\n  [status],\n)\n\n// After\nuseLiveQuery({\n  query: (q) =>\n    q\n      .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n      .where(({ todo }) => eq(todo.status, status)),\n})\n```\n\nIf the query uses opaque functional variants, add `queryKey`:\n\n```tsx\nuseLiveQuery({\n  queryKey: [todoCollection.id, 'status-fn', status],\n  query: (q) =>\n    q\n      .from({ todo: todoCollection })\n      .fn.where(({ todo }) => todo.status === status),\n})\n```\n\n### 6. Preload and dehydrate on the server\n\nPreload a collection when the browser should receive normalized source rows:\n\n```tsx\nconst dbClient = new DbClient()\nconst todos = dbClient.collection(todoCollection)\nawait todos.preload()\n\nreturn {\n  dbState: dbClient.dehydrate(),\n}\n```\n\nPreload a live query when the browser only needs the rendered result:\n\n```tsx\nconst dbClient = new DbClient()\nawait dbClient.preloadLiveQuery(openTodosQuery)\n\nreturn {\n  dbState: dbClient.dehydrate(),\n}\n```\n\n### 7. Hydrate before client hooks read DB\n\n```tsx\n<DbProvider client={client}>\n  <HydrationBoundary state={loaderData.dbState}>\n    <App />\n  </HydrationBoundary>\n</DbProvider>\n```\n\nImperative integrations can call `client.hydrate(loaderData.dbState)` before\nrendering instead.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nNo existing public API is removed by this change.\n\nStill supported:\n\n- `createCollection(...)`\n- passing collection instances to `useLiveQuery(...)`\n- `useLiveQuery(queryFn, deps)`\n- `useLiveSuspenseQuery(queryFn, deps)`\n- mutation APIs such as `insert`, `update`, `delete`, `subscribe`, and\n  optimistic mutation helpers\n\nWarnings:\n\n- React dependency arrays warn in development and will be removed in 1.0.\n- Opaque query IR without `queryKey` warns in development and keeps legacy\n  mount-stable identity until 1.0. In 1.0 it will throw.\n- Expensive derived identity warns in development and suggests `queryKey`.\n\nRequired for SSR:\n\n- stable explicit collection ids\n- request-scoped server `DbClient`\n- browser-scoped client `DbClient`\n- `DbProvider` for descriptor resolution in React\n- `dehydrate()` on the server and `hydrate()` in the browser\n\nRequired for render-time Suspense streaming:\n\n- `routerWithDbClient(router, dbClient)`\n- `useLiveSuspenseQuery(...)` inside a Suspense boundary\n- a stable derived query identity or explicit serializable `queryKey`\n\n## Detailed Changelog\n\n### Added\n\n- `DbClient`\n- `collectionOptions(...)`\n- `CollectionOptions` descriptor type\n- `CollectionMaterializeOptions`\n- `DehydratedDbState`\n- `DehydratedCollectionChunk`\n- `DehydratedCollectionRow`\n- `dbClient.collection(descriptor, options?)`\n- `dbClient.dehydrate()`\n- `dbClient.hydrate(state)`\n- `dbClient.applyCollectionChunk(chunk)`\n- `dbClient.subscribe(listener)`\n- `dbClient.createTransaction(config)`\n- `dbClient.cleanup()`\n- React `DbProvider`\n- React `useDbClient()`\n- React `useOptionalDbClient()`\n- React `HydrationBoundary`\n- React descriptor resolution inside live query builders\n- React derived structured query identity\n- React `queryKey` escape hatch for opaque or hot-path queries\n- React per-query `client` override\n- SSR-capable `useSyncExternalStore` server snapshot support\n- `dbClient.preloadLiveQuery(...)`\n- Svelte `DbProvider`, `useDbClient()`, descriptor resolution, and synchronous\n  server snapshot support\n- TanStack Start and Next.js Playwright SSR E2E coverage\n- `@tanstack/react-router-with-db`\n- render-time `useLiveSuspenseQuery` promise streaming\n\n### Changed\n\n- React `useLiveQuery({ query })` can use collection descriptors directly in\n  `from`, `join`, `leftJoin`, and `unionAll` sources when a `DbProvider` is\n  present.\n- React live query identity is derived from normalized structured IR when no\n  explicit `queryKey` or legacy dependency array is supplied.\n- Explicit collection preloading serializes normalized collection rows.\n- Live-query preloading and render-time discovery serialize ordered result\n  snapshots without implicitly serializing source collections.\n- Browser observers keep the hydrated result visible while normal source sync\n  starts, then publish one authoritative handoff.\n- Hydration applies rows as committed synced state without invoking mutation\n  handlers or creating optimistic state.\n- Hydration and adapter sync begin in a deterministic order: pending rows and\n  sync metadata are imported before sync starts.\n- `DbClient` owns collection instances and ambient transaction scope; cleanup\n  releases both.\n- Incremental chunks use the same collection payload shape as full dehydration.\n- Streamed live-query promises resolve to live-query result snapshots.\n\n### Deprecated\n\n- React dependency arrays for `useLiveQuery` and wrappers that delegate to it.\n  They still work and warn in development. They are planned for removal in 1.0.\n\n### Not Changed\n\n- `createCollection(...)` remains available.\n- Direct collection runtime APIs remain available.\n- Vue, Solid, and Angular keep their existing dependency/reactivity model until\n  they get their own SSR/client-provider work. Svelte is covered by this change.\n- Query collection `queryKey` is still TanStack Query's cache key. It is\n  separate from React live query identity.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe SSR strategy is covered by:\n\n- core `DbClient` tests for hydration, streaming chunks, sync metadata,\n  initial data precedence, explicit ids, and no optimistic serialization\n- React tests for `DbProvider`, descriptor resolution, derived query identity,\n  `queryKey`, deprecation warnings, SSR result snapshots, and atomic handoff\n- Svelte tests for provider ownership, server snapshot rendering, and browser\n  handoff\n- query adapter tests to ensure Query cache behavior still holds\n- persistence core tests to ensure persisted row behavior remains intact\n- TanStack Start and Next.js Playwright E2Es that verify a Suspense fallback,\n  streamed query result, omitted source-only data, clean hydration, and atomic\n  replacement by browser sync\n"}
